A||||16||Slammed Fiero||3.1ltr cavalier motor||||1||
Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||02-02-2001||06:41 PM||||Alrighty ...... Through a good fiero friend I have the oppertunity to aquire a 3.1ltr cavalier motor , complete with the exception of the upper intake manifold.<P>My understanding is that I can't use the Aluminum heads on the motor if I want to use the fiero injection , But I can use fiero iron heads on the block. <P>Someone care to elaborate on the aluminum head issue???<P><BR>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||ironhedno3||02-02-2001||08:07 PM||||if you use the 3.1 short block with iron heads and the aluminun head piston it wont have enough compression..best bet is to use the iron head camaro/firebird piston||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||02-02-2001||09:41 PM||||Hey, today I raced a 3.1 cavelier and man did he ever spank me!  He was gone man...do u guys suggtest I go with a 3.1 for a engine swap?<BR>thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sideview.jpg">  </A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shaun41178||02-02-2001||10:07 PM||||you put your fiero heads on that 3.1 cavalier motor and it won't run good.  It will make less power then what you have now.  REason: compression ratio will be too low.  i computed it and it came to under 7:1 compression.  I think it was actually around 6.8:1.  No good there.  Don't do it unless you plan on rebuilding it and using the proper pistons for the iron head engines<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||02-03-2001||01:56 AM||||This is the motor I plan to use in my turbo project , so perhaps a low compresssion ratio isn't so bad.  With the proper work I can run a comp ratio of 8.5:1 , plus a turbo at 14psi boost , good setup.<P>The whole motor for Free-99<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FieroGTRacingInc||02-03-2001||07:44 AM||||Can you change to the correct piston's(for 2.8L head's) without having to do a complete rebuild?? I have never done a rebuild of any motor, How hard is it using some sort of manual or something??? <BR>Thank's for the input!!!!<BR>  Steve...<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phaeton||02-03-2001||11:26 AM||||The pistons can be changed with the heads and oil pan off.  The cam, crank, and end covers won't have to come off, saving some time.<BR>But think about this, for half again as much time all the bearings could be replaced and new crosshatching could be scratched onto the cylinders.  New pistons deserve a refurbished home to live in, its only fair.<P>Necessary items are lotsa tools, a book, and a buddy that will stick it out for the entire run.||||reg||12
Z||000007||1FieroGTRacingInc||02-03-2001||12:29 PM||||So a total rebuild is the best... that's what I thought! My MAIN QUESTIONIS...  Is the 3.1L swap really worth the $$$$$?  Do you ACTUALLY really gain that much performance, compared to the money you spend for .3L gain???  thank's.<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phaeton||02-03-2001||12:47 PM||||The rod/stroke ration of the 3.1 gives more dwell time at TDC and the longer stroke puts out more torque.  The first makes a difference at the ragged edge of camshaft duration when running way over seven grand.  The second will help at street performance levels, passing acceleration at WOT will be stronger.<BR>Worth the cost?  That's a mental question.||||reg||12
Z||000009||rogergarrison||02-03-2001||03:36 PM||||I used a Cavalier Z24 block and bottom end. used the 2.8 heads milled and stock Fiero intake plenum. Used new 2.8 pistons and came up with a little over 8-1 compression ... thats what most turbo manufacturers recommend. Mine runs fine, screams to 6500RPM. Not a rocket out of the hole, but when its wound up. I get some valve float around 6800.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||02-03-2001||04:13 PM||||when it comes to being worth the cost , probably not... I want a 3.2ltr motor , hypernumatic pistons , a cam , stainless valves , ported and polished heads , the whole deal... when it's all said and done I could probably use a basic archie kit with an IRon head V8 and a carb..but it just won't be the same....<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Slammed Fiero||02-03-2001||04:16 PM||||forgot to mention , this will be the base for my turbo setup.<P>Jonathan ||||reg||1
Z||000012||1FieroGTRacingInc||02-03-2001||09:48 PM||||So it's NOT REALLY WORTH THE COST??? all opinion's welcome on this.....  thank's!!!<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Will||02-04-2001||11:04 AM||||This isn't really on topic, but I raced a 3.1 Beretta up a mountain once. I flat left him in the corners, but he was pulling pretty hard in the straights.<P>Slammed:<BR>     I thought you wanted a ZZ4? Am I confusing you with Seanh in that respect?<P>1FieroGTRacingInc:<BR>     Couldn't you have come up with a shorter name? As I said above, the 3.1 Beretta was pulling pretty hard in the straights. For the ease of a swap, I think a stock 3.1 is worth the money.<BR>     If you tear the engine down, you'll need to do a hi-po rebuild to make it worth the money/trouble (~190 hp).<BR>     If you go turbo, you'll need to do a turbo specific (low compression) rebuild to be able to run enough boost to make it worth your money/trouble (~300hp).<BR>     That is assuming that you are good mechanically and can do a lot of your own work.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Slammed Fiero||02-04-2001||12:16 PM||||Ease of swap is the reason. Yeah I looked at the ZZ4 for a while , but I have to be serious , I have an 18,000 mile 87 Corvette sitting in the garage , original owner Koni's ,Borla exhaust Doug Nash 4+3, gulstrand suspension , for cost sake I could put a ZZ4 in that and build up the injection. All this would cost a lot less than a Fiero V8 swap and yield the same results with a better chassis under the car.  I guess it's just a personal decisions due to my circumstances.<P>I have always been intrigued with turbo's, We had a 66 corvair with a 180 turbo and a merkur running 18psi boost , both cars were an enormous amount of fun. the merkur went 100,000 miles before the head gasket needed to be replaced and the turbo needed to be rebuilt. This was 100,000 of 2 teenagers driving the car , my brother and I.<P>So thats the reason I scrapped the small block idea...for now. I will have a V8 someday. The corvette just sits there , my dad lost intrest in it when he got his RS.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||COUNTIBLIS||02-04-2001||12:39 PM||||I have a 3.1 beretta aluminum head engine, that was dropped in my car last week!  Let me tell you, if you do it, you wont regret it.  You have better top end power, to me it feels like better torque, and the exhaust sounds damn good!  If you do this though you need to get the wiring for the donor, the ecm, and some other things, I think like the flywheel also to balance it.  I dont know much of the swap, my mechanic did most of it.  But here are some pics.  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine2_1.jpg"> <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine3.JPG"> <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine1_2.jpg"> <P><BR>Good Luck!<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count3.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||COUNTIBLIS||02-04-2001||12:41 PM||||I know the engine is dirty, but it has been so damn cold that I havent been able to do anything to her. <P><BR>||||reg||1
